with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about most consumers of lemon soda."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The coloring enhances something for them."}, {"n": 4, "text": "What is enhanced is their enjoyment."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The enjoyment is of the beverage."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "This particular additive should not be banned, therefore, because its benefits greatly outweigh its risks.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about this particular additive."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It says the additive should not be banned."}, {"n": 4, "text": "A reason is given."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The reason is that benefits outweigh risks."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The outweighing is described as great."}]}], "the_read": "What if enjoyment is not a health-related benefit?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q7", "qnum": 7, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 8, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q8", "prompt": "Fines levied against those responsible for certain environmentally damaging accidents are now so high that it costs a company responsible for such an accident more to pay the fine than it would have cost to adopt measures that would have prevented the accident. Therefore, since businesses value their profits, those that might have such accidents will now install adequate environmental safeguards.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about fines. · The fines are levied against those responsible for accidents. · The accidents are environmentally damaging ones. · This applies to certain accidents, not all. · The fines are now very high. · Paying the fine costs a company more. · The comparison is with the cost of preventive measures. · Those measures would have prevented the accident. (2) This is the conclusion. · A reason is given for it. · The reason is that businesses value their profits. · It is about businesses that might have such accidents. · They will install environmental safeguards. · The safeguards are described as adequate. · This is predicted to happen now.", "category": "Weaken", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Fines levied against those responsible for certain environmentally damaging accidents are now so high that it costs a company responsible for such an accident more to pay the fine than it would have cost to adopt measures that would have prevented the accident.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about fines."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The fines are levied against those responsible for accidents."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The accidents are environmentally damaging ones."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This applies to certain accidents, not all."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The fines are now very high."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Paying the fine costs a company more."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The comparison is with the cost of preventive measures."}, {"n": 8, "text": "Those measures would have prevented the accident."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Therefore, since businesses value their profits, those that might have such accidents will now install adequate environmental safeguards.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "A reason is given for it."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The reason is that businesses value their profits."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It is about businesses that might have such accidents."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They will install environmental safeguards."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The safeguards are described as adequate."}, {"n": 7, "text": "This is predicted to happen now."}]}], "the_read": "What if businesses think they''ll never have an accident so there''s no need to invest in safeguards?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q8", "qnum": 8, "question_type": "Weaken", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 9, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q9", "prompt": "Even in a democracy, it is necessary to restrict the dissemination of advanced technological knowledge that is of commercial or national-security value. Dissemination to certain countries, those that are or will be competitors or enemies, should be selectively prohibited. There must, however, be free exchange of scientific information.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This concedes something about democracies. · Restricting dissemination is necessary. · What is restricted is advanced technological knowledge. · The knowledge has commercial value. · It may instead have national-security value. (2) This is about dissemination to certain countries. · Those countries are competitors or enemies. · They may be so now or in the future. · Dissemination should be prohibited. · The prohibition is selective rather than total. (3) This is a contrast with what came before. · Something must be the case. · There must be free exchange. · What is exchanged is scientific information.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Even in a democracy, it is necessary to restrict the dissemination of advanced technological knowledge that is of commercial or national-security value.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This concedes something about democracies."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Restricting dissemination is necessary."}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is restricted is advanced technological knowledge."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The knowledge has commercial value."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It may instead have national-security value."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Dissemination to certain countries, those that are or will be competitors or enemies, should be selectively prohibited.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about dissemination to certain countries."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Those countries are competitors or enemies."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They may be so now or in the future."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Dissemination should be prohibited."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The prohibition is selective rather than total."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "There must, however, be free exchange of scientific information.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Something must be the case."}, {"n": 3, "text": "There must be free exchange."}, {"n": 4, "text": "What is exchanged is scientific information."}]}], "the_read": "There must be scientific information that is not advanced technological knowledge.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q9", "qnum": 9, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 10, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q10", "prompt": "Water vapor evaporated from the ocean contains a greater proportion of oxygen-16 and a smaller proportion of the heavier oxygen-18 than does seawater. Normally, this phenomenon has no effect on the overall composition of the ocean, because evaporated seawater returns to the ocean through precipitation. During an ice age, however, a large amount of precipitation falls on ice caps, where it is trapped as ice.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about water vapor. · The vapor was evaporated from the ocean. · It contains a greater proportion of oxygen-16. · It contains a smaller proportion of oxygen-18. · Oxygen-18 is the heavier of the two. · The comparison is with seawater. (2) This describes what happens normally. · The phenomenon has no effect. · What is unaffected is the ocean''s overall composition. · A reason is given for that. · Evaporated seawater returns to the ocean. · It returns through precipitation. (3) This is a contrast with the normal case. · It describes what happens during an ice age. · Precipitation falls on ice caps. · The amount is large. · The precipitation is trapped there. · It is trapped as ice.", "category": "Most Strongly Supported", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Water vapor evaporated from the ocean contains a greater proportion of oxygen-16 and a smaller proportion of the heavier oxygen-18 than does seawater.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about water vapor."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The vapor was evaporated from the ocean."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It contains a greater proportion of oxygen-16."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It contains a smaller proportion of oxygen-18."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Oxygen-18 is the heavier of the two."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The comparison is with seawater."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Normally, this phenomenon has no effect on the overall composition of the ocean, because evaporated seawater returns to the ocean through precipitation.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This describes what happens normally."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The phenomenon has no effect."}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is unaffected is the ocean''s overall composition."}, {"n": 4, "text": "A reason is given for that."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Evaporated seawater returns to the ocean."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It returns through precipitation."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "During an ice age, however, a large amount of precipitation falls on ice caps, where it is trapped as ice.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with the normal case."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It describes what happens during an ice age."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Precipitation falls on ice caps."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The amount is large."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The precipitation is trapped there."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It is trapped as ice."}]}], "the_read": "Ice caps formed during an ice age will have a greater proportion of oxygen-16 and a smaller proportion of oxygen-18.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q10", "qnum": 10, "question_type": "Most Strongly Supported", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 11, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q11", "prompt": "Some of the most prosperous nations in the world have experienced a pronounced drop in national savings rates—the percentage of after-tax income an average household saves. This trend will undoubtedly continue if the average age of these nations’ p