stomers."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The railroad serves neither well."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Neither is served particularly well."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Therefore, if a railroad is going to be a successful business, then it must concentrate exclusively on one of these two markets.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is a conditional statement."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The condition is being a successful business."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The railroad must concentrate on one market."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The concentration must be exclusive."}, {"n": 6, "text": "There are two markets to choose between."}]}], "the_read": "What if a railroad can serve its customers poorly but still be a successful business?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q18", "qnum": 18, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 18, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q19", "prompt": "Most people in the United States view neither big nor small business as particularly efficient or dynamic and regard both as providing consumers with fairly priced goods and services. However, most people consistently perceive small business as a force for good in society, whereas big business is perceived as socially responsible only in times of prosperity.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about most people. · Those people are in the United States. · They view neither big nor small business as efficient. · They do not view either as dynamic. · Neither is seen as particularly so. · They regard both as providing fairly priced goods. · Services are included as well. · What is provided goes to consumers. (2) This is a contrast with what came before. · It is about most people again. · They perceive small business as a force for good. · That perception is consistent. · The good is in society. · Big business is perceived differently. · It is seen as socially responsible only sometimes. · That is in times of prosperity.", "category": "Most Strongly Supported", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Most people in the United States view neither big nor small business as particularly efficient or dynamic and regard both as providing consumers with fairly priced goods and services.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about most people."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Those people are in the United States."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They view neither big nor small business as efficient."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They do not view either as dynamic."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Neither is seen as particularly so."}, {"n": 6, "text": "They regard both as providing fairly priced goods."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Services are included as well."}, {"n": 8, "text": "What is provided goes to consumers."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "However, most people consistently perceive small business as a force for good in society, whereas big business is perceived as socially responsible only in times of prosperity.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about most people again."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They perceive small business as a force for good."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That perception is consistent."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The good is in society."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Big business is perceived differently."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It is seen as socially responsible only sometimes."}, {"n": 8, "text": "That is in times of prosperity."}]}], "the_read": "Businesses can be perceived as a force for good in society even if they are not perceived as being particularly dynamic.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q19", "qnum": 19, "question_type": "Most Strongly Supported", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 19, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q20", "prompt": "The energy an animal must expend to move uphill is proportional to its body weight, whereas the animal’s energy output available to perform this task is proportional to its surface area. This is the reason that small animals, like squirrels, can run up a tree trunk almost as fast as they can move on level ground, whereas large animals tend to slow down when they are moving uphill.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about an animal. · It is about energy the animal must expend. · The energy is for moving uphill. · That energy is proportional to something. · It is proportional to body weight. (2) This is a contrast with what came before. · It is about the animal''s energy output. · That output is the amount available. · It is available to perform this task. · It is proportional to surface area. (3) This states a reason for what follows. · It is about small animals. · Squirrels are given as the example. · They can run up a tree trunk. · They do it almost as fast as on level ground. · The comparison is with level ground. (4) This is a contrast with the small animals. · It is about large animals. · They tend to slow down. · This is a tendency rather than a rule. · It happens when they are moving uphill.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "The energy an animal must expend to move uphill is proportional to its body weight,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about an animal."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about energy the animal must expend."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The energy is for moving uphill."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That energy is proportional to something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It is proportional to body weight."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "whereas the animal’s energy output available to perform this task is proportional to its surface area.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about the animal''s energy output."}, {"n": 3, "text": "That output is the amount available."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It is available to perform this task."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It is proportional to surface area."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "This is the reason that small animals, like squirrels, can run up a tree trunk almost as fast as they can move on level ground,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This states a reason for what follows."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about small animals."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Squirrels are given as the example."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They can run up a tree trunk."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They do it almost as fast as on level ground."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The comparison is with level ground."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "whereas large animals tend to slow down when they are moving uphill.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with the small animals."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about large animals."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They tend to slow down."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This is a tendency rather than a rule."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It happens when they are moving uphill."}]}], "the_read": "What if small animals have a much smaller surface area to body weight ratio than large animals?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q20", "qnum": 20, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 20, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q21", "prompt": "The 1980s have been characterized as a period of selfish individualism that threatens the cohesion of society. But this characterization is true of any time. Throughout history all human actions have been motivated by selfishness. When the deeper implications are considered, even the simplest “unselfish” acts prove to be instances of selfish concern for the human species.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about the 1980s. · That decade has been characterized in a certain way. · It is called a period of selfish individualism. · That individualism threatens something. · What is threatened is the cohesion of society. (2) This is a contrast with what came before. · It is about that characterization. · The characterization is true. · It is true of any time, not just the 1980s. (3) This covers the whole of history. · It is about human actions. · It applies to all of them. · They have been motivated by selfishness. (4) This depends on considering deeper implications. · It is about unselfish acts. · It applies even to the simplest of them. · Those acts prove to be something else. · They are instances of selfish concern. · The concern is for the human species.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "The 1980s have been characterized as a period of selfish individualism that threatens the cohesion of society.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about the 1980s."}, {"n": 2, "text": "That decade has been characterized in a certain way."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It is called a period of selfish individualism."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That individualism threatens something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "What is threatened is the cohesion of society."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "But this characterization is true of any time.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about that characterization."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The characterization is true."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It is true of any time, not just the 1980s."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Throughout history all human actions have been motivated by selfishness.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This covers the whole of history."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about human actions."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It applies to all of them."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They have been motivated by selfishness."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "When the deeper implications are considered, even the simplest “unselfish” acts prove to be instances of selfish concern for the human species.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This depends on considering deeper implications."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about unselfish acts."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It applies even to the simplest of them."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those acts prove to be something else."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They are instances of selfish concern."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The concern is for the human species."}]}], "the_read": "What if selfish individualism is different from selfish concern for human species?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q21", "qnum": 21, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 21, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q22", "prompt": "A medical journal used a questionnaire survey to determine whether a particular change in its format would increase its readership. Sixty-two percent of those who returned the questionnaire supported that change. On the basis of this outcome, the decision was made to introduce the new format.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a medical journal. · The journal used a survey. · The survey was a questionnaire. · It was used to determine something. · The question was about a change in format. · The change is a particular one. · The issue is whether it would increase readership. (2) This gives a figure. · The figure is sixty-two percent. · It is a percentage of a specific group. · The group is those who returned the questionnaire. · Those people supported the change. (3) This rests on that outcome. · A decision was made. · The decision was to introduce the new format.", "category": "Strengthen", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "A medical journal used a questionnaire survey to determine whether a particular change in its format would increase its readership.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a medical journal."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The journal used a survey."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The survey was a questionnaire."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It was used to determine something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The question was about a change in format."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The change is a particular one."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The issue is whether it would increase readership."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Sixty-two percent of those who returned the questionnaire supported that change.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This gives a figure."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The figure is sixty-two percent."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It is a percentage of a specific group."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The group is those who returned the questionnaire."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those people supported the change."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "On the basis of this outcome, the decision was made to introduce the new format.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This rests on that outcome."}, {"n": 2, "text": "A decision was made."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The decision was to introduce the new format."}]}], "the_read": "What if the sample size of those who returned the survey is too small? What if the people who are in favor of the change are disproportionately sampled among those who returned the survey?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q22", "qnum": 22, "question_type": "Strengthen", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 22, "slug": "PT1_S3_Q23", "prompt": "Shanna: Owners of any work of art, simply by virtue of ownership, ethically have the right to destroy that artwork if they find it morally or aesthetically distasteful, or if caring for it becomes inconvenient.\n\nJorge: Ownership of unique artworks, unlike ownership of other kinds of objects, carries the moral right to possess but not to destroy. A unique work of art with aesthetic or historical value belongs to posterity and so must be preserved, whatever the personal wishes of its legal owner.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) The first speaker is named Shanna. · She is talking about owners. · The owners are of any work of art. · Their claim rests on ownership alone. (2) The owners have a right. · The right is an ethical one. · The right is to destroy the artwork. · It applies under certain conditions. · One is finding it morally distasteful. · Another is finding it aesthetically distasteful. · Another is caring for it becoming inconvenient. (3) The second speaker is named Jorge. · He is talking about ownership of unique artworks. · He contrasts that with other kinds of objects. · That ownership carries a moral right. · The right is to possess the artwork. · The right does not extend to destroying it. (4) This is about a unique work of art. · The work has aesthetic or historical value. · It belongs to posterity. · It must therefore be preserved. · That holds whatever the owner wishes. · The owner in question is the legal owner.", "category": "Counter", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Shanna: Owners of any work of art, simply by virtue of ownership,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The first speaker is named Shanna."}, {"n": 2, "text": "She is talking about owners."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The owners are of any work of art."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Their claim rests on ownership alone."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "ethically have the right to destroy that artwork if they find it morally or aesthetically distasteful, or if caring for it becomes inconvenient.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The owners have a right."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The right is an ethical one."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The right is to destroy the artwork."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It applies under certain conditions."}, {"n": 5, "text": "One is finding it morally distasteful."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Another is finding it aesthetically distasteful."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Another is caring for it becoming inconvenient."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Jorge: Ownership of unique artworks, unlike ownership of other kinds of objects, carries the moral right to possess but not to destroy.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The second speaker is named Jorge."}, {"n": 2, "text": "He is talking about ownership of unique artworks."}, {"n": 3, "text": "He contrasts that with other kinds of objects."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That ownership carries a moral right."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The right is to possess the artwork."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The right does not extend to destroying it."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "A unique work of art with aesthetic or historical value belongs to posterity and so must be preserved, whatever the personal wishes of its legal owner.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a unique work of art."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The work has aesthetic or historical value."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It belongs to posterity."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It must therefore be preserved."}, {"n": 5, "text": "That holds whatever the owner wishes."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The owner in question is the legal owner."}]}], "the_read": "The speakers disagree over whether art owners have the right to destroy any of their artworks.", "the_read_type": "C", "questions": [{"citation": "PT1.S3.Q23", "qnum": 23, "question_type": "Counter", "correct_answer": "E"}, {"citation": "PT1.S3.Q24", "qnum": 24, "question_type": "Controversy", "correct_answer": "A"}]}]'::jsonb,
