nt''s reputation has gone down. (3) This is the conclusion. · It rests on those facts. · The facts are called conclusive evidence. · The claim is about Professor Smythe''s appointment. · He was appointed for a purpose. · The purpose was to undermine the department.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Since Professor Smythe has been head of the department, the most distinguished member of the faculty has resigned,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This covers a period of time."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The period is since Professor Smythe became head."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Smythe is head of the department."}, {"n": 4, "text": "A member of the faculty has resigned."}, {"n": 5, "text": "That member was the most distinguished one."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "fewer new courses have been developed, student enrollment has dropped, and the reputation of the department has gone down.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This adds more things that happened."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Fewer new courses have been developed."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Student enrollment has dropped."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The department''s reputation has gone down."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "These facts provide conclusive evidence that Professor Smythe was appointed to undermine the department.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It rests on those facts."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The facts are called conclusive evidence."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The claim is about Professor Smythe''s appointment."}, {"n": 5, "text": "He was appointed for a purpose."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The purpose was to undermine the department."}]}], "the_read": "What if Professor Smythe''s appointment didn''t cause any of these negative events? What if just because all of these things happened after Smythe''s appointment, that doesn''t mean it was intentional?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q5", "qnum": 5, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 6, "