tion_type": "Resolution", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 8, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q8", "prompt": "Eva: A “smart highway” system should be installed, one that would monitor areawide traffic patterns and communicate with computers in vehicles or with programmable highway signs to give drivers information about traffic congestion and alternate routes. Such a system, we can infer, would result in improved traffic flow in and around cities that would do more than improve drivers’ tempers; it would decrease the considerable loss of money and productivity that now results from traffic congestion.\n\nLuis: There are already traffic reports on the radio. Why would a “smart highway” system be any better?", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) The first speaker is named Eva. · She is talking about a system. · The system is called a smart highway. · She says it should be installed. (2) The system would monitor traffic patterns. · The patterns are areawide. · The system would also communicate. · It could communicate with computers in vehicles. · It could instead communicate with programmable highway signs. · The purpose is to give drivers information. · The information is about traffic congestion. · It is also about alternate routes. (3) This is stated as something we can infer. · The system would improve traffic flow. · The improvement is in and around cities. · It would do more than one thing. · Improving drivers'' tempers is not all of it. (4) The system would decrease a loss. · The loss is of money. · The loss is also of productivity. · The loss is considerable. · It results from traffic congestion. · This is happening now. (5) The second speaker is named Luis. · He points out something that already exists. · Traffic reports exist already. · The reports are on the radio. (6) This is a question. · The question is about the smart highway system. · It asks why the system would be better. · It doubts that it would be better at all.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Eva: A “smart highway” system should be installed,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The first speaker is named Eva."}, {"n": 2, "text": "She is talking about a system."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The system is called a smart highway."}, {"n": 4, "text": "She says it should be installed."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "one that would monitor areawide traffic patterns and communicate with computers in vehicles or with programmable highway signs to give drivers information about traffic congestion and alternate routes.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The system would monitor traffic patterns."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The patterns are areawide."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The system would also communicate."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It could communicate with computers in vehicles."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It could instead communicate with programmable highway signs."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The purpose is to give drivers information."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The information is about traffic congestion."}, {"n": 8, "text": "It is also about alternate routes."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Such a system, we can infer, would result in improved traffic flow in and around cities that would do more than improve drivers’ tempers;", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is stated as something we can infer."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The system would improve traffic flow."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The improvement is in and around cities."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It would do more than one thing."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Improving drivers'' tempers is not all of it."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "it would decrease the considerable loss of money and productivity that now results from traffic congestion.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The system would decrease a loss."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The loss is of money."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The loss is also of productivity."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The loss is considerable."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It results from traffic congestion."