r whether reducing the highway speed limit would cause illegal behavior.", "the_read_type": "C", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q16", "qnum": 16, "question_type": "Controversy", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 15, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q17", "prompt": "People cannot devote themselves to the study of natural processes unless they have leisure, and people have leisure when resources are plentiful, not when resources are scarce. Although some anthropologists claim that agriculture, the cultivation of crops, actually began under conditions of drought and hunger, the early societies that domesticated plants must first have discovered how the plants they cultivated reproduced themselves and grew to maturity. These complex discoveries were the result of the active study of natural processes.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) People cannot study natural processes without leisure. · Devoting themselves is what requires it. · People have leisure when resources are plentiful. · They do not have it when resources are scarce. (2) This is a contrast. · Some anthropologists make a claim. · The claim is about agriculture. · Agriculture is the cultivation of crops. · They say it began under conditions of drought. · They say it began under hunger too. (3) This is about early societies. · Those societies domesticated plants. · They must have made discoveries first. · They discovered how the plants reproduced themselves. · They discovered how the plants grew to maturity. · The plants meant are the ones they cultivated. (4) The discoveries were complex. · They were the result of study. · The study was active. · What was studied is natural processes.", "category": "Inference", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "People cannot devote themselves to the study of natural processes unless they have leisure, and people have leisure when resources are plentiful, not when resources are scarce.", "details": [{"n": 