 went to pay for standard methods of treatment, which are known to be effective though they are expensive and painful. An increasing percentage is being spent on nonstandard treatments, which cause little discomfort. Unfortunately, the nonstandard treatments have proved to be ineffective. Obviously, less money is being spent now on effective treatments of disease X than was spent ten years ago.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about the past decade. · A percentage of money is decreasing. · The money is spent on treating disease X. · That percentage pays for standard methods of treatment. (2) The standard methods are known to be effective. · This is a contrast. · The standard methods are expensive. · The standard methods are painful. (3) A percentage is increasing. · It is spent on nonstandard treatments. · Those treatments cause discomfort. · The discomfort is little. (4) This is marked as unfortunate. · It is about the nonstandard treatments. · They have proved ineffective. (5) This is the conclusion. · It is treated as obvious. · Less money is being spent now. · The money is for effective treatments of disease X. · The comparison is with what was spent ten years ago.", "category": "Sufficient Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "In the past decade, a decreasing percentage of money spent on treating disease X went to pay for standard methods of treatment,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about the past decade."}, {"n": 2, "text": "A percentage of money is decreasing."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The money is spent on treating disease X."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That percentage pays for standard methods of treatment."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "which are known to be effective though they are expensive and painful.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The standard methods are known to be effective."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The standard methods are expensive."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The standard methods are painful."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "An increasing percentage is being spent on nonstandard treatments, which cause little discomfort.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "A percentage is increasing."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is spent on nonstandard treatments."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those treatments cause discomfort."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The discomfort is little."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Unfortunately, the nonstandard treatments have proved to be ineffective.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is marked as unfortunate."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about the nonstandard treatments."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They have proved ineffective."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "Obviously, less money is being spent now on effective treatments of disease X than was spent ten years ago.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is treated as obvious."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Less money is being spent now."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The money is for effective treatments of disease X."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The comparison is with what was spent ten years ago."}]}], "the_read": "What if we''re spending more money overall on treating disease X?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q18", "qnum": 18, "question_type": "Sufficient Assumption", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 17, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q19", "prompt": "When an ordinary piece of steel is put under pressure, the steel compresses; that is, its volume slightly decreases. Glass, however, is a fluid, so rather than compressing, it flows when put under pressure; its volume remains unchanged. Any portion of a sheet of glass that is under sustained pressure will very slowly flow to areas under less pressure. Therefore, if a single, extremely heavy object is placed in the middle of a horizontal sheet of glass of uniform thickness and if the glass is able to support the weight without cracking, then the sheet of glass will eventually _______.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a piece of steel. · The steel is an ordinary one. · It is put under pressure. · What happens is the steel compresses. · A definition of that follows. · The steel''s volume decreases. · The decrease is slight. (2) This is a contrast. · Glass is a fluid. · A consequence is drawn from that. · Glass does not compress. · Glass flows instead of compressing. · It flows when put under pressure. · Its volume remains unchanged. (3) This is about a portion of a sheet of glass. · It holds for any such portion. · The portion is under pressure. · The pressure is sustained. · The portion will flow. · It flows very slowly. · It flows to areas under less pressure. (4) This is the conclusion. · An object is placed on the glass. · There is only one object. · The object is extremely heavy. · It is placed in the middle of the sheet. · The sheet is horizontal. · The sheet is of uniform thickness. · The glass supports the weight without cracking.", "category": "Fill In", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "When an ordinary piece of steel is put under pressure, the steel compresses; that is, its volume slightly decreases.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a piece of steel."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The steel is an ordinary one."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It is put under pressure."}, {"n": 4, "text": "What happens is the steel compresses."}, {"n": 5, "text": "A definition of that follows."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The steel''s volume decreases."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The decrease is slight."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Glass, however, is a fluid, so rather than compressing, it flows when put under pressure; its volume remains unchanged.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Glass is a fluid."}, {"n": 3, "text": "A consequence is drawn from that."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Glass does not compress."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Glass flows instead of compressing."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It flows when put under pressure."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Its volume remains unchanged."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Any portion of a sheet of glass that is under sustained pressure will very slowly flow to areas under less pressure.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a portion of a sheet of glass."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It holds for any such portion."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The portion is under pressure."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The pressure is sustained."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The portion will flow."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It flows very slowly."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It flows to areas under less pressure."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Therefore, if a single, extremely heavy object is placed in the middle of a horizontal sheet of glass of uniform thickness and if the glass is able to support the weight without cracking, then the sheet of glass will eventually _______.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "An object is placed on the glass."}, {"n": 3, "text": "There is only one object."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The object is extremely heavy."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It is placed in the middle of the sheet."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The sheet is horizontal."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The sheet is of uniform thickness."}, {"n": 8, "text": "The glass supports the weight without cracking."}]}], "the_read": "The glass will eventually be thicker at the edges and thinner under the heavy object.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q19", "qnum": 19, "question_type": "Fill In", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 18, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q20", "prompt": "Anyone who insists that music videos are an art form should also agree that television gave rise to an art form, since television gave rise to music videos.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about anyone with a certain view. · The view is that music videos are an art form. · Such a person insists on it. · That person should also agree to something. · They should agree television gave rise to an art form. · This is the reason given. · Television gave rise to music videos.", "category": "Parallel Reasoning", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Anyone who insists that music videos are an art form should also agree that television gave rise to an art form, since television gave rise to music videos.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about anyone with a certain view."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The view is that music videos are an art form."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Such a person insists on it."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That person should also agree to something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They should agree television gave rise to an art form."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is the reason given."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Television gave rise to music videos."}]}], "the_read": "What if the rules of conditional reasoning don''t apply?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q20", "qnum": 20, "question_type": "Parallel Reasoning", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 19, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q21", "prompt": "Medieval Arabs had manuscripts of many ancient Greek texts, which were translated into Arabic when there was a demand for them. Medieval Arab philosophers were very interested in Aristotle''s Poetics, an interest that evidently was not shared by medieval Arab poets, because a poet interested in the Poetics would certainly have wanted to read Homer, to whose epics Aristotle frequently refers. But Homer was not translated into Arabic until modern times.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Medieval Arabs had manuscripts. · The manuscripts were of ancient Greek texts. · There were many of them. · The texts were translated into Arabic. · Translation happened when there was demand. (2) Medieval Arab philosophers were interested in a text. · The text is Aristotle''s Poetics. · The interest was very great. · Medieval Arab poets did not share it. · This is marked as evident. (3) This is the reason given. · It is about a poet interested in the Poetics. · Such a poet would have wanted to read Homer. · This is stated with certainty. · Aristotle refers to Homer''s epics. · Aristotle refers to them frequently. (4) This is a contrast. · Homer was not translated into Arabic. · This held until modern times.", "category": "Strengthen", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Medieval Arabs had manuscripts of many ancient Greek texts, which were translated into Arabic when there was a demand for them.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Medieval Arabs had manuscripts."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The manuscripts were of ancient Greek texts."}, {"n": 3, "text": "There were many of them."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The texts were translated into Arabic."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Translation happened when there was demand."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Medieval Arab philosophers were very interested in Aristotle''s Poetics, an interest that evidently was not shared by medieval Arab poets,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Medieval Arab philosophers were interested in a text."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The text is Aristotle''s Poetics."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The interest was very great."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Medieval Arab poets did not share it."}, {"n": 5, "text": "This is marked as evident."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "because a poet interested in the Poetics would certainly have wanted to read Homer, to whose epics Aristotle frequently refers.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the reason given."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about a poet interested in the Poetics."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Such a poet would have wanted to read Homer."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This is stated with certainty."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Aristotle refers to Homer''s epics."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Aristotle refers to them frequently."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "But Homer was not translated into Arabic until modern times.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Homer was not translated into Arabic."}, {"n": 3, "text": "This held until modern times."}]}], "the_read": "What if medieval Arab poets read Homer in Greek?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q21", "qnum": 21, "question_type": "Strengthen", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 20, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q22", "prompt": "Congenial guests and a plentiful supply of good things to eat and drink will ensure a successful dinner party. Since Sylvia has prepared more than enough to eat and drink and her guests are all congenial people, her dinner party is certain to be a success.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Two things will ensure something. · One is congenial guests. · The other is a supply of good things to eat and drink. · The supply is plentiful. · What is ensured is a dinner party''s success. (2) This is the reason given. · Sylvia has prepared enough to eat and drink. · She has prepared more than enough. · Her guests are congenial people. · All of them are. · This is the conclusion. · Her dinner party will be a success. · This is stated as certain.", "category": "Parallel Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Congenial guests and a plentiful supply of good things to eat and drink will ensure a successful dinner party.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two things will ensure something."}, {"n": 2, "text": "One is congenial guests."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The other is a supply of good things to eat and drink."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The supply is plentiful."}, {"n": 5, "text": "What is ensured is a dinner party''s success."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Since Sylvia has prepared more than enough to eat and drink and her guests are all congenial people, her dinner party is certain to be a success.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the reason given."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Sylvia has prepared enough to eat and drink."}, {"n": 3, "text": "She has prepared more than enough."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Her guests are congenial people."}, {"n": 5, "text": "All of them are."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Her dinner party will be a success."}, {"n": 8, "text": "This is stated as certain."}]}], "the_read": "What if Sylvia''s cooking sucks?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q22", "qnum": 22, "question_type": "Parallel Flaw", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 21, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q23", "prompt": "A museum director, in order to finance expensive new acquisitions, discreetly sold some paintings by major artists. All of them were paintings that the director privately considered inferior. Critics roundly condemned the sale, charging that the museum had lost first-rate pieces, thereby violating its duty as a trustee of art for future generations. A few months after being sold by the museum, those paintings were resold, in an otherwise stagnant art market, at two to three times the price paid to the museum. Clearly, these prices settle the issue, since they demonstrate the correctness of the critics'' evaluation.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) A museum director sold paintings. · The paintings are by major artists. · Only some were sold. · The selling was discreet. · The purpose was to finance new acquisitions. · The acquisitions are expensive. (2) This is about all of the paintings sold. · The director considered them inferior. · The director did so privately. (3) Critics condemned the sale. · The condemnation was round. · They made a charge. · The charge is that the museum lost first-rate pieces. · Doing so violated a duty. · The duty is as a trustee of art. · The art is held for future generations. (4) The paintings were resold. · This was a few months after the museum sold them. · The art market was otherwise stagnant. · The resale price was higher. · It was two to three times higher. · The comparison is with the price paid to the museum. (5) This is the conclusion. · It is treated as clear. · The prices settle the issue. · This is the reason given. · The prices demonstrate something. · What they demonstrate is that the critics'' evaluation was correct.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "A museum director, in order to finance expensive new acquisitions, discreetly sold some paintings by major artists.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "A museum director sold paintings."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The paintings are by major artists."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Only some were sold."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The selling was discreet."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The purpose was to finance new acquisitions."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The acquisitions are expensive."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "All of them were paintings that the director privately considered inferior.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about all of the paintings sold."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The director considered them inferior."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The director did so privately."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Critics roundly condemned the sale, charging that the museum had lost first-rate pieces, thereby violating its duty as a trustee of art for future generations.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Critics condemned the sale."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The condemnation was round."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They made a charge."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The charge is that the museum lost first-rate pieces."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Doing so violated a duty."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The duty is as a trustee of art."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The art is held for future generations."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "A few months after being sold by the museum, those paintings were resold, in an otherwise stagnant art market, at two to three times the price paid to the museum.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The paintings were resold."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This was a few months after the museum sold them."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The art market was otherwise stagnant."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The resale price was higher."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It was two to three times higher."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The comparison is with the price paid to the museum."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "Clearly, these prices settle the issue, since they demonstrate the correctness of the critics'' evaluation.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is treated as clear."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The prices settle the issue."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This is the reason given."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The prices demonstrate something."}, {"n": 6, "text": "What they demonstrate is that the critics'' evaluation was correct."}]}], "the_read": "What if a high price doesn''t mean something is a great work of art? What if an obnoxious rich person bought these for the express purpose of laughing at how bad they are?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q23", "qnum": 23, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 22, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q24", "prompt": "The United States ranks far behind countries such as Sweden and Canada when it comes to workplace safety. In all three countries, joint labor-management committees that oversee workplace safety conditions have been very successful in reducing occupational injuries. In the United States, such committees are found only in the few companies that have voluntarily established them. However, in Sweden and several Canadian provinces, joint safety committees are required by law and exist in all medium-sized and large workplaces.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about the United States. · It ranks behind other countries. · It ranks far behind. · Sweden is one of them. · Canada is another of them. · The subject is workplace safety. (2) This holds in all three countries. · There are joint labor-management committees. · The committees oversee workplace safety conditions. · The committees have been successful. · They have been very successful. · What they reduced is occupational injuries. (3) This returns to the United States. · Such committees are found only in some companies. · Those companies are few. · Those companies established them voluntarily. (4) This is a contrast. · This is about Sweden. · It is also about Canadian provinces. · Several provinces are meant. · Joint safety committees are required by law. · They exist in all medium-sized workplaces. · They exist in all large workplaces.", "category": "Inference", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "The United States ranks far behind countries such as Sweden and Canada when it comes to workplace safety.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about the United States."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It ranks behind other countries."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It ranks far behind."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Sweden is one of them."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Canada is another of them."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The subject is workplace safety."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "In all three countries, joint labor-management committees that oversee workplace safety conditions have been very successful in reducing occupational injuries.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This holds in all three countries."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There are joint labor-management committees."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The committees oversee workplace safety conditions."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The committees have been successful."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They have been very successful."}, {"n": 6, "text": "What they reduced is occupational injuries."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "In the United States, such committees are found only in the few companies that have voluntarily established them.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This returns to the United States."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Such committees are found only in some companies."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those companies are few."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those companies established them voluntarily."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "However, in Sweden and several Canadian provinces, joint safety committees are required by law and exist in all medium-sized and large workplaces.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This is about Sweden."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It is also about Canadian provinces."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Several provinces are meant."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Joint safety committees are required by law."}, {"n": 6, "text": "They exist in all medium-sized workplaces."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They exist in all large workplaces."}]}], "the_read": "There is some correlation between legally mandated joint safety committees and better workplace safety.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q24", "qnum": 24, "question_type": "Inference", "correct_answer": "A"}]}]'::jsonb,
