{"n": 2, "text": "One might expect something of the first kind of contract."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Final costs can exceed original cost estimates."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Such excess would be more common there."}]}, {"n": 6, "text": "Paradoxically, such cost overruns are actually more common if the contract is of the fixed-profit kind.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is presented as a paradox."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about such cost overruns."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The overruns are actually more common."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This holds if the contract is of the fixed-profit kind."}]}], "the_read": "What if clients are more likely to review and negotiate down construction costs when the contractor''s fee is tied to the overall cost?", "the_read_type": "R", "questions": [{"citation": "PT103.S1.Q23", "qnum": 23, "question_type": "Resolution", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 23, "slug": "PT103_S1_Q24", "prompt": "That wall is supported by several joists. The only thing that can have caused the bulge that the wall now has is a broken joist. Therefore, at least one of the joists is broken.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a particular wall. · The wall is supported by joists. · There are several joists. (2) This is about a bulge. · The wall now has that bulge. · Something caused the bulge. · Only a broken joist can have caused it. (3) This is the conclusion. · It is about the joists. · At least one of them is broken.", "category": "Parallel Reasoning", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "That wall is supported by several joists.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a particular wall."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The wall is supported by joists."}, {"n": 3, "text": "There are several joists."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "The only thing that can have caused the bulge that the wall now has is a broken joist.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a bulge."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The wall now has that bulge."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Something caused the bulge."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Only a broken joist can have caused it."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Therefore, at least one of the joists is broken.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about the joists."}, {"n": 3, "text": "At least one of them is broken."}]}], "the_read": "What is the rules of conditional reasoning don''t apply?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT103.S1.Q24", "qnum": 24, "question_type": "Parallel Reasoning", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 24, "slug": "PT103_S1_Q25", "prompt": "Sasha: Handwriting analysis should be banned in court as evidence of a person''s character: handwriting analysts called as witnesses habitually exaggerate the reliability of their analyses.\n\nGregory: You are right that the current use of handwriting analysis as evidence is problematic. But this problem exists only because there is no licensing board to set professional standards and thus deter irresponsible analysts from making exaggerated claims. When such a board is established, however, handwriting analysis by licensed practitioners will be a legitimate courtroom tool for character assessment.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Sasha is the first speaker. · This is her recommendation. · Handwriting analysis should be banned. · The ban would be in court. · It is used as evidence of a person''s character. (2) This is her reason. · It is about handwriting analysts. · Those analysts are called as witnesses. · They exaggerate the reliability of their analyses. · They do so habitually. (3) Gregory is the second speaker. · He agrees with part of what Sasha said. · The current use of handwriting analysis is problematic. · That use is as evidence. (4) This is a contrast with what he granted. · The problem exists for one reason only. · There is no licensing board. · Such a board would set professional standards. · The standards would deter irresponsible analysts. · Those analysts make exaggerated claims. (5) This is his conclusion. · Such a board may be established. · Handwriting analysis would then be legitimate. · The analysis would be done by licensed practitioners. · It would be a courtroom tool. · The tool would be for character assessment.", "category": "Method", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Sasha: Handwriting analysis should be banned in court as evidence of a person''s character:", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Sasha is the first speaker."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This is her recommendation."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Handwriting analysis should be banned."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The ban would be in court."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It is used as evidence of a person''s character."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "handwriting analysts called as witnesses habitually exaggerate the reliability of their analyses.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is her reason."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about handwriting analysts."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those analysts are called as witnesses."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They exaggerate the reliability of their analyses."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They do so habitually."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Gregory: You are right that the current use of handwriting analysis as evidence is problematic.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Gregory is the second speaker."}, {"n": 2, "text": "He agrees with part of what Sasha said."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The current use of handwriting analysis is problematic."}, {"n": 4, "text": "That use is as evidence."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "But this problem exists only because there is no licensing board to set professional standards and thus deter irresponsible analysts from making exaggerated claims.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what he granted."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The problem exists for one reason only."}, {"n": 3, "text": "There is no licensing board."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Such a board would set professional standards."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The standards would deter irresponsible analysts."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Those analysts make exaggerated claims."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "When such a board is established, however, handwriting analysis by licensed practitioners will be a legitimate courtroom tool for character assessment.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is his conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Such a board may be established."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Handwriting analysis would then be legitimate."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The analysis would be done by licensed practitioners."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It would be a courtroom tool."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The tool would be for character assessment."}]}], "the_read": "The speakers disagree over whether handwriting analysis should be banned no matter what.", "the_read_type": "C", "questions": [{"citation": "PT103.S1.Q25", "qnum": 25, "question_type": "Method", "correct_answer": "B"}, {"citation": "PT103.S1.Q26", "qnum": 26, "question_type": "Counter", "correct_answer": "D"}]}]'::jsonb,
